18. SECURITY RULES AND BACKEND

Security is a mandatory part of the project.

Implement and document restrictive Firebase Realtime Database Security Rules.

Requirements:

- Deny unauthenticated access to private user data.
- Users can read only their own private profile and histories.
- Users cannot directly change wallet balances.
- Users cannot directly mark purchases as verified.
- Users cannot assign themselves Admin roles.
- Admin access must be enforced by trusted authorization.
- Package writes require authorized admin privileges.
- Sensitive audit logs cannot be edited by normal clients.
- Validate input types and allowed fields.
- Never deploy open read/write rules.

Use a trusted backend, such as secured Firebase Cloud Functions or an equivalent server environment, for:

- Google Play purchase verification.
- Wallet credits and debits.
- Purchase token deduplication.
- Refund/revocation processing.
- Admin authorization.
- Admin UID management.
- Account status changes.
- Audit log generation.

The Firebase Admin SDK bypasses Realtime Database Security Rules, so the backend must explicitly validate authentication, authorization, inputs, and transaction conditions.

Do not put backend secrets inside HTML, JavaScript, an Android asset, or a publicly accessible Firebase node.

